And you're going to have a lot of refined controls

00:39:11.904 --> 00:39:13.904
over who you share with.

00:39:13.904 --> 00:39:15.944
So at the content level,

00:39:15.944 --> 00:39:18.423
you can invite specific people in

00:39:18.423 --> 00:39:20.464
that are within your organization.

00:39:20.464 --> 00:39:24.263
So these are either viewers or publishers or admins

00:39:24.263 --> 00:39:27.423
within my organization's account here, right?

00:39:28.024 --> 00:39:30.823
So I could add, let's go ahead and add Amy.

00:39:31.944 --> 00:39:33.944
Amy just got an email that said,

00:39:33.944 --> 00:39:36.583
hey, Amy, you've been invited to this piece of content,

00:39:36.583 --> 00:39:37.863
you know, go check it out.

00:39:37.863 --> 00:39:40.504
So now she is a viewer on this account.

00:39:40.504 --> 00:39:42.703
If I wanted to promote her, if she had the rights,

00:39:42.703 --> 00:39:45.863
I could also make her a publisher if I wanted to, right?

00:39:45.863 --> 00:39:48.823
If she's a publisher, sorry, an editor.

00:39:48.823 --> 00:39:50.624
If she's an editor, she can change things

00:39:50.624 --> 00:39:52.663
like the things about the deployment itself,

00:39:52.663 --> 00:39:55.383
the compute resources, some of the metadata.

00:39:55.383 --> 00:39:56.224
So you want to be careful

00:39:56.263 --> 00:39:57.663
with the content that you're assigning.

00:39:57.663 --> 00:39:59.543
If you want to invite people

00:39:59.543 --> 00:40:01.663
at your whole organization level,

00:40:01.663 --> 00:40:03.423
then I could say, well, let's bring everybody in

00:40:03.423 --> 00:40:04.423
as a viewer.

00:40:04.423 --> 00:40:07.184
And then anybody who has viewer privileges or above

00:40:07.184 --> 00:40:09.263
is now able to see this piece of content.

00:40:10.143 --> 00:40:11.624
If I have the public use case,

00:40:11.624 --> 00:40:13.784
and I want everyone in the world to be able to see it,

00:40:13.784 --> 00:40:16.624
I can change public access to enabled.

00:40:18.344 --> 00:40:20.064
So those are like the internal

00:40:20.064 --> 00:40:21.304
and the public sharing use case.

00:40:21.304 --> 00:40:24.143
But the really interesting one with Connect Cloud

00:40:24.143 --> 00:40:26.583
is that we have this notion of external guest.

00:40:26.583 --> 00:40:27.823
And I know for a lot of you,

00:40:27.823 --> 00:40:30.184
especially people who do consulting, right?

00:40:30.184 --> 00:40:32.543
You might have five different clients

00:40:32.543 --> 00:40:34.143
and each client has three or four people

00:40:34.143 --> 00:40:36.103
that need to come in and eventually see something

00:40:36.103 --> 00:40:38.103
that you've made for them as a one-off handoff,

00:40:38.103 --> 00:40:40.143
or maybe it's a recurring analytics dashboard

00:40:40.143 --> 00:40:41.983
that they're constantly going into.

00:40:41.983 --> 00:40:46.504
You also have this notion of external guest on Connect Cloud.

00:40:46.504 --> 00:40:49.904
So if I were to invite in someone externally

00:40:49.904 --> 00:40:51.703
that is not in my system right now,

00:40:51.703 --> 00:40:53.143
so you can see everybody here

00:40:54.224 --> 00:40:55.703
has been brought in at the account level.

00:40:55.703 --> 00:40:59.583
But if I wanted to add in somebody externally,

00:40:59.583 --> 00:41:03.024
maybe add a new client at alex.dataquery.com,

00:41:03.024 --> 00:41:05.983
now this person just got an email

00:41:05.983 --> 00:41:08.744
that says you've been invited by this organization

00:41:08.744 --> 00:41:13.024
to Connect Cloud to view this specific piece of content.

00:41:13.024 --> 00:41:15.504
They would need to come to Connect Cloud.

00:41:15.504 --> 00:41:16.344
They would need to,

00:41:16.344 --> 00:41:18.224
if they don't already have a free account,

00:41:18.224 --> 00:41:21.504
create a free account through Google or GitHub

00:41:22.263 --> 00:41:23.263
or email and password.

00:41:23.263 --> 00:41:25.583
And now this person, once they accept,

00:41:25.583 --> 00:41:26.543
they would log in.

00:41:26.543 --> 00:41:27.663
And the only thing that they would see

00:41:27.663 --> 00:41:30.704
would be this one specific thing that we shared with them.

00:41:31.863 --> 00:41:34.903
They're actually not a member of your internal account.

00:41:34.903 --> 00:41:39.903
So they don't have a role of publisher or admin or viewer.

00:41:40.264 --> 00:41:43.384
They're explicitly denoted as an external viewer

00:41:43.384 --> 00:41:46.223
tied to one or more pieces of content.

00:41:47.184 --> 00:41:49.543
So that's kind of like the levels of cascading sharing

00:41:49.543 --> 00:41:51.944
you can do within Connect Cloud.

00:41:51.944 --> 00:41:53.423
And then at the admin level here,

00:41:53.423 --> 00:41:54.264
let's see if we have,

00:41:54.264 --> 00:41:56.023
yeah, you can see like we have specific people

00:41:56.023 --> 00:41:58.543
who are named as a guest within this account.

00:41:59.983 --> 00:42:02.584
So we try to give as much control as possible there.

00:42:06.304 --> 00:42:07.144
Excellent.

